# Phase 18 ChangeInvisibleTimeRequestHeader nullable decode — 2026-10-18

- Continued the P18-V01 header audit on
  `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate-resume`. Read the pinned
  RocketMQ Java source at `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; this
  request header uses reflective decoding under both hints, has nullable
  string/wrapper fields, primitive `suspend=false`, and a no-op `checkFields`.
- Added a pinned invoked Java fixture for missing fields, malformed and
  overflowing numbers, valid Arabic-Indic digits, both decode hints, and
  re-encoded fields. Rust now represents nullable header fields with `Option`,
  preserves unset fields on encode, and maps success-path missing `offset`,
  `topic`, or `queueId` to typed header errors. Non-success replies retain
  Java's `NoExist` branch without reading those request fields.
- Code/fixture commit: `8f64dde3 fix(protocol): preserve nullable
  change-invisibility headers`. Documentation is committed separately.
